-- Ordered quest guidance; source 967020b2b8ca645afcaf90d9bbe5a1b64673947d; generated 2026-10-20.
QuestGuidance.Register("en",166,{
[5281]="7002AF5D\n1\tBuild one of Virgil's snowmen\tIn the field outside of Winter-home, select the style of snowman you'd like to build.\n2\tTalk to Virgil Greenfield\t\n",
[5282]="700370A0\n1\tDefeat Eldnoth\tThe brigand leader may be found in the marshes east of Oserley. Dudsig has asked you to find and defeat the leader of the brigands who assaulted Lúfa.\n2\tTalk to Dudsig in Oserley\tDudsig is near the stables in Oserley, west of the marshes. You should return to Dudsig with news of your success.\n",
[5283]="7001C4E6\n1\tSearch treasure-piles for relics of worth (total: 10)\tThe ruins of Dannenglor are north of the Haunted Inn, in the Dourstocks. You should search the Elf-ruins of Dannenglor for any treasures that might recall the Elves of old.\n2\tTalk to Mírdiniel at the Haunted Inn\tMírdiniel awaits you in the Haunted Inn, south of Dannenglor. You should speak with Mírdiniel and inform her that there was nothing to be found among the morroval-hoards in Dannenglor.\n",
[5284]="70054CA6\n1\tCollect lost relics (total: 8)\tLost relics can be found in Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-well. You should collect lost relics.\n2\tReturn to Ereblen\tEreblen can be found at Echad Uial. You should bring the lost relics to Ereblen.\n",
[5285]="70054CA2\n1\tGather the remnants of Rauniel (total: 3)\tRemnants of Rauniel can be found in Eithel Gwaur, the Filth-well. You should gather the remnants of Rauniel.\n2\tReturn to Ereblen\tEreblen can be found at Echad Uial. You should bring the remnants of Rauniel to Ereblen.\n",
[5286]="70054CA7\n1\tAdd pure water to the source of the Morgulduin (quantity: see journal)\tThe waters of the Morgulduin are deadly at its source. You should attempt to purify the deadly waters of the Morgulduin River.\n2\tCompleted\t\n",
[5287]="7006AA07\n1\tDefeat Ilmabiri rats (total: 6)\tSewer rats can be found throughout Ilmabiri, but may be more plentiful in Gedma-ghâr, on the eastern edge.\n2\tTalk to Gajóta\tYou have slain many Ilmabiri rats. Return to Gajóta to let him know.\n",
[5288]="7002BF8C\n1\tTalk to Ulferth at Atburg in the Rushgore\tUlferth can be found at the edge of Atburg, south-east of Aculf's camp in the Rushgore. Aculf asked you to deliver his ultimatum to Ulferth, captain of the treasure-seekers in the Rushgore.\n2\tTalk to Eowils outside Atburg in the Rushgore\tEowils is outside Atburg in the Rushgore, south-east of Aculf's camp. Aculf instructed you to bring Ulferth's answer to the scout Eowils.\n",
[5289]="70028263\n1\tDefeat wights in the eastern valley (total: 10)\tWights can be found among the cairns east along the road above the Bone Quarry. Naeglanc has asked you to banish any wights you might find around the cairns in the eastern valley.\n2\tTalk to Mair among the cairns\tMair can be found in the eastern valley above the Bone Quarry. Naeglanc asked you to speak with Mair.\n",
[5290]="70035F43\n1\tSpeak with Thrymm\tGárwig, Thrymm and Cyneberg have gathered in the Mead Hall in Forlaw to prepare for the final stand against Núrzum. Speak with Thrymm and let him know you are ready to end Núrzum's path of destruction once and for all.\n2\tSpeak with Thrymm in the Forlaw Mead Hall\tThrymm has returned to the Forlaw Mead Hall. You should speak with him after the great victory.\n",
[5291]="70007764\n1\tSearch for Malin\tThe journal you found seemed to indicate that Malin was taken to the southern Barrow-downs to a barrow overlooking an evil mire. Addie Wheatley has asked you to search for her other son, Malin.\n2\tTalk to Addie Wheatley at the Dead Man's Perch\tAddie Wheatley awaits your return at the relative safety offered by her guides at the Dead Man's Perch. In your search of the Barrow-downs, you found both of Addie's sons, Amlach and Malin, but far too late to be of any help to either. The foul creatures of the Barrow-downs had killed them both and took Malin's remains for their own. You should return to Addie Wheatley and tell her what has happened to her son.\n",
[5292]="7006B717\n1\tTalk to Agalûnu\tShanthar has thanked you for all that you have done. He asked you to visit Agalûnu once more to check on her and tell her he will visit soon.\n2\tReturn to Kalkhadra in Iridír\tYou have bid Agalûnu farewell and she asked you to tell her sister Kalkhadra in Iridír that she is all right.\n",
[5293]="70071CCF\n1\tSearch for clues to Baradûm's whereabouts. Galêris mentioned he was last seen patrolling near the caves of Jâr Obadal. Jâr Obadal can be found south-east of Ingar-garâsh.\t\n2\tSearch for Baradûm in Jâr Obadal\tSearch for Baradûm in Jâr Obadal.\n3\tCheck the body to determine if it is Baradûm\tCheck the body to determine if it is Baradûm.\n4\tReturn to Galêris with the news of Baradûm's death\tReturn to Galêris with the news of Baradûm's death.\n",
[5294]="70067F92\n1\tRaghda-gûn asked you to find Berkha in Irkhadâr, the caldera lake in Zamarzîr. Irkhadâr is north of Aklâradum.\t\n2\tFind Berkha\tRaghda-gûn asked you to find Berkha in Irkhadâr, the caldera lake in Zamarzîr. Irkhadâr is north of Aklâradum.\n3\tTalk to Berkha\tBerkha announced his presence at the shore of Irkhadâr. Speak to Berkha.\n4\tTalk to Raghda-gûn\tYou have found little Berkha and should take him back to Aklâradum. Aklâradum is on a cliff to the south of Irkhadâr.\n",
[5295]="70066858\n1\tTraps can be found outside the hamlet of Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. Dírion has asked you to search the traps outside Alagrant for any sign of 'Blue', a beloved toy of his dog, Draug. You should search the traps in the woods around Alagrant.\t\n2\tFree 'Blue' from the sprung trap\tThe sprung trap can be found outside Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. You have found a small blue object caught in one the traps. You should free 'Blue' from the trap.\n3\tDeliver 'Blue' to Draug in Alagrant\tDraug can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. You have found 'Blue' in one of the traps outside Alagrant. You should return 'Blue' to Draug in Alagrant.\n4\tTalk to Dírion\tDírion can be found in Alagrant, in the Blackroot Vale. You have returned 'Blue' to Draug and he appears pleased. You should talk to Dírion.\n",
[5296]="70069DF3\n1\tPick tart berries (total: 8)\tPick tart berries that grow to the west of where Barhador is camped in the Angle of Mitheithel.\n2\tReturn to Barhador with the tart berries\tReturn to Barhador at his camp in the Angle of Mitheithel with the berries you picked.\n",
[5297]="7006B70D\n1\tCollect healing herbs (total: 4)\tAgalûnu has asked you to collect healing herbs for a poultice. They can be found across the stream to the south-east.\n2\tMix the herbs with a mortar and pestle\tYou have collected herbs to make a healing poultice for Agalûnu. You should mash them with the mortar and pestle near Agalûnu's tent.\n3\tApply the poultice\tYou have made a healing poultice. You should go to Agalûnu and apply it to her wound.\n4\tTalk to Agalûnu\tYou have made a healing poultice and applied it to Agalûnu's wound. You should talk to her and see how she is doing.\n5\tTalk to Shanthar\tAgalûnu must rest to allow her wound to heal. In the meantime, she asked you to return to Shanthar and reassure him that she intends to keep her promise to help him care for the forest. Shanthar is at his abode in Arwáth.\n",
[5298]="7002CB70\n1\tLocate the entrance of the spider-cave\tVenom-bite spider-cave lies west of Landroval's hidden clearing. Landroval has requested that you discover the entrance to the spider-lair he viewed to the west.\n2\tEnter the cave and search for Meneldor\tVenom-bite spider-cave lies west of Landroval's hidden clearing. Landroval has asked you to search inside the spider-lair for his missing friend, Meneldor.\n3\tTalk to Landroval\tLandroval can be found at the clearing of trees in the north-east section of the Wailing Hills. Landroval awaits your return and will be eager to see his friend Meneldor as well.\n",
[5299]="7000371B\n1\tTalk to Atli Spider-bane in Archet\tAtli Spider-bane can be found just north of Cal Sprigley. Cal Sprigley suggested that you speak with Atli Spider-bane about the spiders at his farm and how to be rid of them.\n2\tSearch for Bali\tThe entrance to the cave the hunters blocked off lies in the ruins due east of Archet. Atli told you that he sent his cousin Bali to check the caves, but he has not yet returned. If you find him, he may have the answer to what has disturbed the spiders.\n3\tUse Cocoon\tThe missing pages of Bali's journal must be somewhere within the caves. The spiders may have taken the missing pages and webbed them into their cocoons. You have found Bali's corpse and his journal, but the journal is missing several pages. You need to find the pages before returning to Atli.\n4\tBring the journal and journal pages to Atli Spider-bane\tAtli Spider-bane can be found at the north end of Archet. Atli Spider-bane will want to know what you discovered among the pages of Bali's journal.\n",
[5300]="7002824F\n1\tSeal cairn-openings (total: 3)\tThe Bone Quarry lies to the east of Echad Naeglanc. Naeglanc has asked you to close several cairn-openings within the Bone Quarry.\n2\tTalk to Ilar at his camp in the Bonevales\tIlar is at his camp, north and east of the Bone Quarry. You should seek out Ilar and let him know that the cairns have been sealed.\n",
[5301]="70044D74\n1\tComplete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Back Door\030Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Invaders\030Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: Kamabhosh\030Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: Treachery\030Complete Quest: Breach in the Darkness: The Withered Foe\tRathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon and assist him with protecting the Cisterns.\n2\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found at the northern end of the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon.\n",
[5302]="70026EF7\n1\tDefeat Red-eye\tRed-eye was said to be at a den to the south-west. Elain has asked you to hunt down Red-eye in her stead while she prepares for the evening's rites.\n2\tTalk to Elain at Lhan Tarren\tElain awaits you in Lhan Tarren. You should speak with Elain and inform her that you slew her old enemy.\n",
[5303]="70071634\n1\tCollect hay bale\tNahíd has requested help gathering his sheep. You should start by collecting the nearby hay bale.\n2\tWhistle at lost sheep (total: 5)\tSeveral sheep have wandered off and become lost in and near Ahâba. You should find and whistle at the lost sheep to send them home.\n3\tTalk to Nahíd\tYou have found all of Nahíd's lost sheep. You should return to Nahíd.\n",
[5304]="7002718D\n1\tFind Yago\030Find Wilim\030Find Matho\030Find Siam\030Find Inir\tYago, Wilim, Siam, Matho, and Inir are lost in the Barnavon Mine. Cada asked you to enter the Barnavon Mine and find the missing miners.\n2\tTalk to Cada at the mine\tCada is at the camp outside the Barnavon Mine. You should return to Cada with news of your success.\n",
[5305]="70000007\n1\tTalk to Shirriff Robin Smallburrow\tRobin Smallburrow can be found at The Ivy Bush Inn in the centre of Hobbiton. Otho thinks that the Shirriffs should be made aware of the danger the spiders may pose and has asked you to speak with Robin Smallburrow, the Shirriff in Hobbiton.\n2\tDefeat spiders (total: 6)\030Find the spiders' nest\tThere may be spiders in the Bindbole Wood, north and north-west of Overhill. Otho Broadbelt sent you to speak with Robin Smallburrow about the spiders, but the Hobbiton Shirriff had already received reports about the creatures in Bindbole Wood. Shirriff Smallburrow has asked you to kill as many of the spiders as you can, but also to find their nest.\n3\tTalk to Shirriff Robin Smallburrow\tRobin Smallburrow can be found in the Ivy Bush in the centre of Hobbiton. Shirriff Smallburrow sent you to deal with the spider threat in Bindbole Wood and to discover the location of their nest. You should report back to Robin Smallburrow with news of your success.\n",
[5306]="7004A8DB\n1\tFollow the trail of the Silent One's blood deeper into Lhingris\tThe trails of blood begin at the Silent Haunt and lead deeper into Lhingris. Legolas has spotted two trails of blood leading from the Silent Haunt. It seems the Silent One is trying to lose you in the shadows of Lhingris.\n2\tTalk to Legolas near Dath Nethryn\tLegolas can be found above the swamp of Dath Nethryn in Lhingris. The trails of blood have led both you and Legolas to the swamp of Dath Nethryn. The Silent One now hides within, hoping to tend his wounds and escape your pursuit.\n",
[5307]="7002D050\n1\tLook for the flags in the field below\030Stand at the edge of the parapets\tThe top of the Eorlsmead Tower will likely be a good vantage point. From the top of the tower, you should look at the land around the tower for range-finding flags.\n",
[5308]="7002C911\n1\tCollect pouches of the Orcs' poison remedy (total: 6)\tMor-hai Orcs can be found within their cave in the western section of the Wailing Hills. Securing remedy from defeated Orcs will likely prove to be a worthwhile endeavour for the Men of Stangard.\n2\tReturn to Penda with the pouches of remedy\tPenda may be found back at the camp, along the road north of the Cuthstan. Frithstan and his men should be able to make good use of the remedy you have collected from the Mor-hai.\n",
[5309]="7002C912\n1\tCollect pouches of the Orcs' poison remedy (total: 6)\tMor-hai Orcs can be found within their cave in the western section of the Wailing Hills. Securing remedy from defeated Orcs will help Frithstan be prepared for further encounters with the Mor-hai.\n2\tReturn to Penda with the pouches of remedy\tPenda may be found back at the camp, along the road north of the Cuthstan. Frithstan and his men should be able to make good use of the remedy you have collected from the Mor-hai.\n",
[5310]="7004463D\n1\tFind and defeat saboteurs (total: 4)\tSaboteurs are hiding in the cisterns. You should defeat the saboteurs.\n2\tSpeak with Rathon\tRathon can be found outside the cistern entrance on the Fourth Circle of Minas Tirith. You should speak with Rathon.\n",
[5311]="700660C8\n1\tSearch for the missing way-stone\tNella has asked you to you look for her missing way-stone. The way-stone went missing in Hashadir.\n2\tReturn to Nella\tYou should bring the way-stone back to Nella. Nella is in Dol Amroth outside of the Swan-knight's Keep.\n",
[5312]="7003707F\n1\tYou should defeat the leaders of the half-orcs near Oserley.\t\n2\tDefeat Rakblog\030Defeat Unaz\tThe leaders of the half-orcs near Oserley roam the field south-west of the village. You should defeat Rakblog and Unaz, leaders of the half-orc scouts near Oserley.\n3\tBring the note you found to Cenulf in Oserley\tCenulf is near the mill in Oserley. You should bring the note you found to Cenulf at once.\n",
})
